 v1=vis('Two questions about a change','Two separate questions distinguish reversibility from substance identity. Melting ice can be reversed by cooling and makes no new substance; tearing paper is difficult to reverse but also makes no new substance.',[txt(40,25,920,55,'Can we undo it? Did it make a new substance?',30,bold=True),rect(50,120,410,290),rect(540,120,410,290),txt(65,140,380,50,'ICE → LIQUID WATER',27,bold=True),txt(565,140,360,50,'PAPER → TORN PAPER',27,bold=True),txt(75,210,360,150,'Cooling can reverse it.\nThe substance is still water.\nPhysical change.',27),txt(565,210,360,150,'Hard to restore the sheet.\nThe paper is still paper.\nPhysical change.',27),txt(55,450,890,70,'Being hard to undo is not enough evidence\nthat a new substance formed.',27)])
